    75	
    76	## Three QC-Compatible Mechanisms to Reuse
    77	
    78	These are **design recommendations, not an empirical guarantee that a redesigned task will fail Opus**. No new domain bundle was authored or certified here.
    79	
    80	1. **Fresh extracts with real interaction witnesses.** Reuse eight fixed variants around an explicit 8-12-stage domain contract, but make each precedence pair decisive. Include equal-ranked conflicts, abutting endpoints, true rounding midpoints and signed residual ties. Grade independent rule-family facts rather than entire report bundles. This retains legitimate generalization pressure while satisfying IN-8/AL-1/AL-27; complete missing output schemas first.
    81	2. **Independent boundary arithmetic as low-weight conduct.** The observed omission is printing plausible outputs without independent expected results, even on a fresh probe. A small, method-neutral criterion for independently validating a genuinely critical boundary or conservation law is defensible. Weight odds-raising conduct as minor (e.g. three), accept equivalent approaches, and avoid seven near-duplicate maximum-weight criteria or mandatory arbitrary probe counts. These changes follow AL-1's conduct split, rather than assuming unannounced habits can carry unlimited weight.
    82	3. **Canonical integrity and preservation checks with proportional credit.** Reuse independent digest/hash-chain recomputation, repeat-run stability and input snapshots. Distinguish invariant semantic outputs from intentionally changed raw input digests. Give these facts their own small budgets, not a repeated dependency in all correctness checks. This retains the observed audit/preservation verification weakness without CL-4 cliffs or impossible manifest comparisons.
